1]Explain indetail about static in java ?
	
	->static is a keyword in java,that can be used with variables,methods,blocks and nested classes,which means
	the members belongs to the class rather than the instance of the class,As a result it can be accessed without
	creating the object for the class.
	
	->To create static vaariables,static methods and static blocks "static" keyword is used with them
	
	->static variables,static methods and static blocks are stored in method area
	
	->The complete program execution will happens in the following sequence
		i)JVM is the process that runs on the Operating system which manages different memory areas like
		method area,stack area and heap area
		ii)JVM gives the control to the class loader,whose duty is to load all static elements into the method
		area,once all the static elements are loaded in method area,the control will be given back to JVM
		JVM will starts execution by executing the static block their after the main() execution starts
		
	->static methods can be invoked by using class name,hence object creation is not required to call the
	static methods
	
	->static block and static method cannot access the non-static variables or instance variables because at
	the time of creating static block and static method the memory for non-static variables or instance 
	variables is not allocated hence they cannot be accessed.
	
		i)static block and static method can access the static variables
		ii)instance block and instance method can access the instance variables
		iii)instance block and instance method can also access the static variables
		iv]static block and static method cannot access the non-static variables or instance variable because
		memory is not allocated.
		
		
Static-Variable
---------------
	1]If a variable is declared inside a class and outside a method with static keyword is called as a static
	variable
	2]static variables are such variables which are common for all the objects hence they are also known as
	class level variables
	3]static variables are intialized with default values automatically
	4]we can use static variables without intializing the values
	5]static variables are stored in method area
	

Static-Block
------------
	1]If we specify a group of statements within a pair of curly braces with static keyword is called as
	static block
	2]The main purpose of the static block is to intialize the static variables
	3]If we want to execute any statements before the main method execution starts then those instructions
	should be kept inside the static block,because static block starts its execution before the main()
	4]We can write any number of static blocks in the program and they get executed in the same order in
	which they has written.
	
	
Static-Method
-------------
	1]If a method is declared with static keyword then it is called as static method
	2]Static methods can be invoked by using class name,hence object creation is not required to call the
	static methods.
	
	

2]Explain what is instance variable ?
	
	->A variable which is declared inside a class and outside a method without anykeyword is called as
	instance variable
	->To access the instance variable value from main() we need to create the object for the class,using
	this object we can access the instance variable value from main() method
	->We can use instance variables without intializing any value
	->Instance variables will be intialized with default values automatically
	->Memory for instance variables is created in heap area
	->Memory for instance variables can be de-allocated by the garbage collector.
	
	

3]Explain what is instance block ?
	
	->If we specify a group of statements with in a pair of curly braces without any keyword is called as
	instance block
	->The main purpose of the instance block is to intialize the instance variables
	->To get execute this instance block object creation must happen
	->We can write any number of instance blocks and they get executed in the same order in which they has 
	written.
	


4]Explain what is instance method ?
	
	->Instance method is a set of instructions written at one place to peform particular task is called as
	instance method
	->A method can also be called as function or module
	->Every method consists of following 4 things:-
		i)MethodName
		ii)Parameters of a method
		iii)Method body or Method defination
		iv)Method return type
	->If a method is not returning anything then the return type should be void
	->If a method returns the value then the return type should be type of the value
	->If a method is not accepting any parameters then it should be left
	->If a method accepts parameters then the respective value or variables should be kept
	inside the parenthesis.	
	->To call instance method we need to create the object for the class.


