9]Explain indetail about access modifiers ?
	
	->Access modifiers are also known as access specifiers in java
	->Access specifiers is used to define the level of accessibility of either the members of class/interface 
	or the level of accessibility of class/interface in a package
	->Java provides 4 level of access modifiers with 3 keywords:-
		1]public access modifier
			->Public access modifier can be accessed anywhere inside the project
			->Public access modifier is used with class,interface,variable,method and constructor
		
		2]protected access modifier
			->Protected access modifier can be accessed anywhere inside the same package and the child class
			of different package
			->Protected access modifier is used with variable,method and constructor
			
		3]default access modifier
			->Default access modifier can be accessed only with the same package,hence it is also known as
			package level access modifier
			->Default access modifier is used with class,interface,variable,method and constructor
		
		4]private access modifier
			->Private access modifier can be accessed only with in the same class
			->Private access modifier is used with variable,method and constructor.
			
			
10]Explain what is final in java ?

	->final is a keyword in java
	->final is used with class,variable and method

final class:-
=============	
->If a class is declared with final keyword then it is called as final class and final class cannot be
extended which means we are not able to perform inheritance on final class.

final variable:-
================
->If a variable is declared with final keyword then it is called as final variable and final variable value
cannot be modified.

final method:-
==============
->if a method is declared with final keyword then it is called as final method and final method cannot be
overriden.

11]Difference between this() method call and this keyword ?
	->"this" keyword is used to resolve the shadowing problem
	->this() is used to call one constructor from another constructor with in the same class.
	

12]Difference between super() method call and super keyword ?  
		->"super" keyword is used to access the parent class instance members like variables,methods and
		constructors from child class constructor or child class instance method
		
		->super() is used to call the parent class constructor from child class constructor 
